      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "2005 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "We report a case of perforation caused by cutting balloon angioplasty of in-stent restenosis in a saphenous vein coronary bypass graft. This was complicated by a subepicardial hematoma leading to avulsion of the penetrating arteries and cardiogenic shock. Despite surgical evacuation and percutaneous left ventricular assist-device support, death ensued."
      },
